# Base URL of the Appealy API, baked into the bundle at build time.
#
# Leave this EMPTY. The console and the API are served from one origin — the
# Vite dev server proxies /auth and /api in development (web/vite.config.ts),
# nginx does the same in the built image (web/nginx.conf) — so the bundle
# should call them as relative, same-origin paths.
#
# That is what keeps the session cookie working. The cookie is SameSite=Lax,
# which means it is only sent on cross-origin requests that are still
# same-site; pointing this at a different hostname than the console is served
# from means the browser silently stops attaching it and every authenticated
# request comes back 401. Note that this is a cookie rule, not a CORS rule —
# allowing the origin in CORS does not make the cookie get sent.
#
# Set an absolute URL here only if you have a deliberate reason to run the two
# as separate origins, and then only if they share a registrable domain
# (console.example.com and api.example.com is fine; two *.run.app hostnames
# are not — run.app is a public suffix, so those count as different sites).
VITE_API_URL=
